          {
            "readme_said": "curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSLf https://termscp.rs/install.sh | sh",
            "actually_needed": "On Debian the script downloads the .deb and installs it with sudo apt/dpkg, which needs root. Without root, download termscp_1.2.2-1_amd64.deb from the GitHub release, extract it with dpkg-deb -x and copy usr/bin/termscp onto PATH. The binary is static, so it runs as is.",
            "kind": "sandbox"
          },
          {
            "readme_said": "(nothing about headless use)",
            "actually_needed": "termscp is TUI-only. To test it without an interactive terminal, run it under `script -qfec` and feed keystrokes through a pipe. In this box the screen output was not captured, so results came from ~/.cache/termscp/termscp.log and from files on disk.",
            "kind": "note"
          },
          {
            "readme_said": "Connect through built-in bookmarks and recent connections",
            "actually_needed": "Connecting with an address on the CLI (termscp ftp://user@host:port) did not add an entry under [recents] in ~/.config/termscp/bookmarks.toml.",
            "kind": "note"
          },
          {
            "readme_said": "Linux users: a keyring manager (optional)",
            "actually_needed": "With no keyring available, termscp logs 'could not instantiate keyring' and falls back to file storage. It keeps working.",
